    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HPXU6B4NHru3Y4nYCDvp77)_\n\n## What\n- `-dryrun` now always previews (writes nothing); `-convert` always applies.\n- Renamed: `sp-notes-filing-lint/-report-apply`, `sp-org-lint-footnotes` (+`-apply`), `sp-litnotes-refs-report`, `sp-litnotes-titles-report/-apply`, `sp-author-notes-preview/-apply`, `sp-bibtex-lint-report/-apply`, `sp-org-normalise-preview/-run`, `sp-org-convert-wikilinks` → `sp-org-wikilinks-convert`, and the vulpea properties preview.\n- New `sp-org-wikilinks-dryrun` (wikilinks had no preview).\n- Old names kept as `define-obsolete-function-alias`.\n- Docs (literate `.org` and tangled `.el`), keybindings and tests use the new names.\n- ADR 0025 records the convention and the full rename table; added to the ADR index.\n- No CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy owns them).\n\n## Not renamed (see ADR)\n- Read-only reports (`sp-org-tag-lint`), `sp-vulpea-convert-keywords` and `sp-vulpea-convert-properties-at-point` (already `convert`, preview inside one run), internal functions.\n\n## Testing\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes; ERT for the touched modules passes in Emacs 29.3 with stubbed dirs. `sp-org-lint-footnote-async-scan-and-apply` fails the same way before and after this change (container limitation).\n- /untested/ on the Mac and the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiChZhAssbXCBtA7kMi)_",
